From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: moniker edge cases (Enum, MonikerCommonPrefixWith, IPersist, composite size/ROT data, MkParseDisplayName syntax)

Moniker edge cases the ole32 conformance tests record from Windows:
IMoniker::Enum with no output pointer is E_INVALIDARG (item, file, class);
MonikerCommonPrefixWith is implemented (it was E_NOTIMPL, so any item, anti or
class moniker prefix against a different moniker failed): two simple monikers
have none (MK_E_NOPREFIX), a simple moniker is compared with a composite's
first component, two composites share their leading components; the file,
anti, composite and pointer monikers no longer answer QueryInterface(IPersist)
and the composite answers its own CLSID; a composite's GetSizeMax counts its
CLSID; a composite holding a pointer moniker has no comparison data (E_NOTIMPL,
length 0); a pointer moniker without an object has no ROT key (E_INVALIDARG);
MkParseDisplayName says MK_E_SYNTAX, not MK_E_CANTOPENFILE, for a name that
cannot be a path (an unknown ProgID, "clsid:"). 18 todo_wine marks removed
from ole32 tests/moniker.c.

---
--- a/dlls/ole32/antimoniker.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/antimoniker.c
